{"name":"Pueblo White","hex":"#e5dfcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pueblo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A community in Spain or Spanish America, especially one of Pueblo Indians living in a stone or adobe multi-storey building. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pueblo"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pueblo","blocks":[{"text":"Pueblo refers to the settlements of the Pueblo peoples, Native American governments in the Southwestern United States, currently in New Mexico, Arizona, and Texas. The permanent communities, including some of the oldest continually occupied settlements in the United States, are called pueblos (lowercased)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Acoma_Pueblo_Sky_City_2.jpg/330px-Acoma_Pueblo_Sky_City_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pueblo"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/500px-Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/500px-Indian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indian Pueblo Cultural Center, Albuquerque, New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndian_Pueblo_Cultural_Center_-_panoramio_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Taospueblo002.jpg/330px-Taospueblo002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Taospueblo002.jpg/330px-Taospueblo002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaospueblo002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/She-we-na_%28Zuni_Pueblo%29_%28Native_American%29._Kachina_Doll_%28Paiyatemu%29%2C_late_19th_century.jpg/500px-She-we-na_%28Zuni_Pueblo%29_%28Native_American%29._Kachina_Doll_%28Paiyatemu%29%2C_late_19th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/She-we-na_%28Zuni_Pueblo%29_%28Native_American%29._K